QSEE TA allocation regression test
----------------------------------
ion_qsee_ta_test is a manually run test for devices exposing the qsecom_ta
heap. It queries the heap by name and tests the 10,952,704-byte gfvenus TA
allocation, page rounding, cached/uncached mmap, zeroing after reuse and
non-overlap with a live small allocation. It exits 4 if the device or heap
is absent, 1 on failure, and 0 on success.

Run as root during a controlled test window with no concurrent TA loading;
the test temporarily consumes roughly 11 MiB of the TA heap. It does not
load firmware, change enrolled fingerprints or restart services. Build it
with the same userspace toolchain as the other ION tests and execute:

  ./ion_qsee_ta_test

For the reserved-pool fix, also check that
/sys/kernel/debug/ion/qsecom_ta/qsecom_ta_stats reports
allocation_mode: reserved. With no other TA allocations, pool_free_bytes
must return to pool_size_bytes after the test. A successful allocation test
alone does not establish that the reservation was enabled or that the
fingerprint HAL successfully loaded its TA.
